{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/763744-identification-within-conspiracies","id":763744,"title":"Identification within Conspiracies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-11T21:39:55-08:00","id":763744,"title":"Identification within Conspiracies","content":"How do members of the conspiracies identify themselves to each other? <br /> <br /> How do they communicate and reveal themselves to each other, or if two agents of the same conspiracy but from different branches ran into each other by accident, how do they reliably figure out friend from foe? Furthermore, how would they detect imposters or spies?<br /> <br /> I know the means and methods would differ greatly from conspiracy to conspiracy, but I was wondering since I don't remember the H:TV book or supplements going into great depth about such things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T03:03:03-08:00","id":764807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if two agents of the same conspiracy but from different branches ran into each other by accident, how do they reliably figure out friend from foe? </div> </div> </div>I imagine some like the Lucifuge just ask. It's a very flat Hierarchy and there's not a great deal to be gained by pretending to be a member.<br /> Highly centralised groups like TFV or Cheiron probably don't worry about it. You will be told if there are other members in the area. If you aren't told then there's a reaon for you not knowing.<br /> I'd say the bigger issues are the large fairly decentralised conspiracies, Ascended Ones, the AKD and MM. If it's a general first meeting, they'd probably try to scope the person out by contacting their local network to confirm that they're legit. If it's a first meeting whilst in the field I'd guess you'd just be extra suspicious until the person has proven themselves. They might have secret handshakes and stuff but that's not terribly safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, how would they detect imposters or spies? </div> </div> </div>Some of the conspiracies have endowements that can solve the problem. I can't remember exactly if the MM have a detect supernatural benediction, but even if they don't it doesn't take a great leap to create the blessing of St. Plotconvenience to solve the problem.<br /> <br /> For others, the very nature of the conspiracy should stop it happening. Cheiron being a a shadowy magical corporation; it doesn't seem a big stretch that infiltrators just vanish. The only infiltration possible in the Lucifuge is really to go meet the Lucifuge herself which is probably a bad idea.<br /> <br /> I imagine TFV aside from their endowements, probably use a lot of counter-intelligence strategies whilst keeping their cells isolated and under heavy surveillance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T10:23:26-08:00","id":765025,"title":"","content":"You pointed out it probably depends a lot on the conspiracies, but it probably depends a lot on the circumstances, too. A hunter isn't likely to just wander to someone's house and ask for help in the hopes of running into another hunter. Generally if you're going to go someplace to meet up with a hunter it's because you've already made an arrangement through connections. Alternatively groups like Cheiron and TFV probably keep databases of identified hunters and arrange for them to assist their own, probably in a method similar to Delta Green, calling them and letting them know they've the opportunity for a 'Night at the Opera.'<br /> <br /> If you're out in the field in the middle of a hunt or about to begin one and you're, for example, checking out a crime scene and you bump into some stranger doing the same thing, acting cautiously hostile until the parties appreciate they're both hunters might work. They might drop terms about the groups they're involved in, or even come clean with everything and hope for the best. But depending on the hunters it might not work. And of course, this leads to a lot of opportunities for monsters to get in. My current werewolf game we've discovered a hunter compact. My character confronted a neutral party who I assumed was a ghoul to learn more about vampires, but as we spoke it slowly dawned that she was actually a vampire hunter and he'd sort of stumbled into introducing himself as a vigilante and getting a proper meeting with the compact that might lead to some sort of recruitment.<br /> <br /> Because of that kind of situation, hunters who can definitively identify monsters are a huge boon and probably considered great assets for compacts. Knowing that, members of any compact could probably get in touch with them with a certain amount of Status. But obviously it can also pay to keep such an ability quiet, for fear of the attention it may bring.<br /> <br /> Hunter is very much a game about stumbling around in the dark, and I think this part of the game is more of that. There's no perfect way to know. The Lucifuge herself could pay you a personal visit and let you know Crooked Tom is coming and he's entirely trustworthy and may need your help for something. But unless she comes with pictures and other evidence of him as a hunter, when the vampire who killed Crooked Tom and took his itinerary arrives claiming to be him, you've no reason to mistrust it. Even if you know what Crooked Tom looks like, someone might have eaten him and is wearing his skin as a disguise. Even if you can absolutely guarantee that it was Crooked Tom, maybe the Lucifuge's information is out of date, and he's just a puppet being controlled by the demon possessing his body. Maybe it wasn't even the Lucifuge, that was probably too good to be true anyways.<br /> <br /> So it's very much a 'be smart, cross your fingers, hope for the best,' kind of game. More paranoid hunters can perform tests, 'Here, touch this silver knife and drink this holy water,' and they're completely justified in doing so, but with the sheer number of different supernaturals out there there's no way for such tests to work across the board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T05:46:34-08:00","id":766193,"title":"","content":"Both are great answers, thanks for the feedback!<br /> <br /> I also assumed that the more decentralized conspiracies might employ certain secret codes and such...was there ever any mention of tattoos or markings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T06:23:47-08:00","id":766207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also assumed that the more decentralized conspiracies might employ certain secret codes and such... </div> </div> </div>That's probably right for the older style conspiracies like the AKD or the Knights of St. George. Though they probably don't rely on them too much, there are too many monsters out there with mind altering/reading powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> was there ever any mention of tattoos or markings? </div> </div> </div>I believe the Ascending Ones do; or at least it's implied they like to use their alchemical symbolism for cool tatoos. There's also the Knights of St. Adrian but that's a special case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:57:47-08:00","id":769404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/763744-identification-within-conspiracies?p=764807#post764807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine TFV aside from their endowements, probably use a lot of counter-intelligence strategies whilst keeping their cells isolated and under heavy surveillance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how much is hinted act, I've suspect that they have a somewhat active history in dealing with infiltration attempts and cleaning up the aftermath. The fact that they know just a bit about High speech and it's relation to ENE lends to how know about these issues. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T17:47:42-08:00","id":772674,"title":"","content":"TF:V also has those RFID chips in their arms - you can have that checked against the database.<br /> <br /> Given that Slashers and other defectors have that shut off (explosively, if I recall correctly)...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T04:25:57-08:00","id":772945,"title":"","content":"I think the whole issue is redundant. I mean come it is crazy to think someone would try to impersonate a member of a top secret organisation that doesn't even exist or if it does hunts things that don't exist. Would you like a tin foil hat to go with you conspiracy-<br /> <br /> <b><i>Oh.</i></b><br /> <br /> Seriously though, I thought it was part and parcel of tier 3 Hunter play. Who are the monsters, who can be trusted...these should always be relevant when you are with one of the Conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T15:15:15-08:00","id":773459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seriously though, I thought it was part and parcel of tier 3 Hunter play. Who are the monsters, who can be trusted...these should always be relevant when you are with one of the Conspiracies. </div> </div> </div>I think that's the point of the thread. It is a threat; so what do the conspiracies do about it? It doesn't need to be foolproof but they need some defences in place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}